from pathlib import Path
import html,json
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
def m(t):return '<div class="math" data-display="true" data-tex="'+html.escape(t,quote=True)+'"></div>'
def links(rows):return '<ul>'+''.join('<li><a href="'+html.escape(u,quote=True)+'">'+html.escape(label)+'</a></li>' for u,label in rows)+'</ul>'
def save(title,body):
 css='body{margin:0;background:#f5f4ee;color:#243331;font:18px/1.65 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1000px;margin:0 auto;padding:40px 24px}h1,h2{font-family:Georgia,serif;line-height:1.2}h1{font-size:2.4rem}a{color:#0b6356}section{border-top:1px solid #c7cfca;padding:25px 0}.math{overflow-x:auto;padding:12px 0}.katex{font-size:1.1em}li{margin:.4em 0}.verdict{background:#dfefe3;padding:20px;border-left:4px solid #0b6356}'
 script='document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>{if(window.katex)el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==="true",throwOnError:false,strict:"ignore",trust:false});}));'
 (HERE/'index.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>'+html.escape(title)+'</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script defer src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js"></script><style>'+css+'</style><script>'+script+'</script></head><body><main>'+body+'</main></body></html>\n')
def main():
 b='<a href="../../index.html#n=20&amp;t=4">← AC-subspace catalogue</a><h1>Fourth-order maximum on twenty qubits</h1>'
 b+='<div class="verdict">'+m(r'K(20,4)=1')+'<p>An exact four-copy certificate excludes every AC4 plane. The existing fifth-order state spans an attaining fourth-order line.</p></div>'
 b+='<section><h2>Attaining exact state</h2>'+m(r'75|\psi\rangle=\sqrt{561}\bigl(|D_{20}^{(0)}\rangle+|D_{20}^{(20)}\rangle\bigr)+3\sqrt{209}\bigl(|D_{20}^{(5)}\rangle-|D_{20}^{(15)}\rangle\bigr)+\sqrt{741}|D_{20}^{(10)}\rangle.')+'<p>This Julia-source state has fifth-order anticoherence, so its one-dimensional span is also fourth-order AC. Its coefficients are normalized because 1122 + 3762 + 741 = 5625.</p>'+links([('../../../anticoherent-state-catalogue/index.html#n=20&t=5&state=acliege-n20-t5','State in the AC-state catalogue'),('../n20-t6/positive-control.json','Independent exact fifth-order verification')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Excluding every plane</h2><p>A hypothetical AC4 plane supplies a positive trace-one invariant moment on the four-copy Young space of shape (2,2), of dimension 16170. The necessary compressed-spin equations give 4253 selected exact equations in 5208 real invariant coordinates.</p><p>An exact rational combination is a strictly positive functional on every nonzero positive moment: all 37 coefficient matrices are positive definite, with 518 strictly positive rational factorization pivots. Hence the moment would have to vanish, contradicting normalization. This covers arbitrary complex planes, and any larger AC4 subspace would contain a plane.</p>'+links([('exclusion/index.html','Detailed exact exclusion'),('exclusion/proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof'),('exclusion/certificate.json','Exact rational certificate'),('exclusion/verify_independently.py','Independent physical reconstruction'),('exclusion/independent-verification.json','Independent verification report')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Neighbouring orders</h2><p>The third-order maximum is two. Fifth-order subspaces have maximum dimension one, and sixth order is impossible. Thus the maximum pure-state AC order on twenty qubits is five.</p>'+links([('../n20-t3/index.html','Third-order analytical plane and optimality'),('../n20-t6/index.html','Sixth-order exclusion')])+'</section>'
 save('Fourth-order maximum on twenty qubits',b)
if __name__=='__main__':main()
